WEBVTT

00:07.620 --> 00:15.630
As I've been teaching PMP Exam preps for a long time and I've taught this all over the U.S. all over

00:15.630 --> 00:23.860
the world and online and noticed a common theme among p.m.-I candidates among PMP candidates and it's

00:24.060 --> 00:30.630
they often have a tendency to over think the questions because there's They want to be so certain to

00:30.630 --> 00:36.210
pass this exam they want to be so certain that they're right that often they look at a question and

00:36.210 --> 00:43.220
they begin to legitimize answers rather than just taking the question at face value.

00:43.530 --> 00:48.760
So you can't read too much into a question you just answer the question.

00:48.930 --> 00:53.280
So don't think too much Don't over think this along that same line.

00:53.280 --> 01:00.490
I've noticed that people who often mail the exam and there have been some folks that don't pass on the

01:00.490 --> 01:08.780
first attempt they tend to be just really dreading the exam and putting it off and putting it off and

01:08.780 --> 01:11.830
they take a long time to prepare.

01:11.840 --> 01:19.280
So I've really come to the conclusion that the longer you take to prepare at some point you have a drop

01:19.280 --> 01:20.020
off.

01:20.030 --> 01:27.320
So I think for most people about four to six weeks is it that you need to have an intense study time

01:27.320 --> 01:28.660
about four to six weeks.

01:28.820 --> 01:36.800
But if you take beyond that I believe there's a risk that your retention and interest really begin to

01:36.800 --> 01:41.450
fade and drop off because you've got life you've got work you've got other things you're interested

01:41.450 --> 01:42.030
in.

01:42.240 --> 01:48.590
And the longer you take to study you're just going to lose touch with things that happen early in the

01:48.590 --> 01:51.080
course and early in your study efforts.

01:51.080 --> 01:56.150
I find that of most people they can compact it to about four to six weeks and that seems like a lot.

01:56.170 --> 01:58.340
But it's really not too bad.

01:58.370 --> 02:01.080
Four to six weeks of intense studying.

02:01.220 --> 02:03.740
And I know you have other commitments and you've got work and so on.

02:03.750 --> 02:10.440
So that may not be realistic for everyone but I would not take a year to study to pass this test.

02:10.490 --> 02:14.360
I would encourage people to try to compact your schedule.

02:14.460 --> 02:16.750
Then don't overthink answers.

02:17.090 --> 02:19.490
But I want you to have confidence that you can do this.

02:19.490 --> 02:20.540
Don't be afraid of this.

02:20.540 --> 02:26.960
I think afraid robs more people of success than failure ever does.

02:27.040 --> 02:27.920
So don't fear this.

02:27.920 --> 02:29.100
This is something you can do.

02:29.180 --> 02:34.950
It's just a test and it's a test that I have confidence you can pass.

02:34.970 --> 02:36.630
So have that confidence.

02:36.830 --> 02:40.440
Don't over think compact your efforts and get it done.

02:40.730 --> 02:42.000
All right keep moving forward.

02:42.130 --> 02:45.660
I'll see you in the next lecture.
